+## The environment checks run in
+Every launcher (`./zn`, the gate, the spec runner) starts what it runs in a fixed environment (c0123, `z-nile/lib/cleanenv.list`): your shell's other variables, functions and `PATH` entries are not passed on. `PATH` becomes `~/.rokit/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`, so `git`, `gh`, `node` and `perl` must be installed in one of those directories (Homebrew, the distribution's packages and Rokit are; a tool from nvm, asdf or nix is not found). A name your setup needs (a proxy, a token) goes in the list in a reviewed change.
